  <h2>The Problem</h2>
  <p>
    Testosterone therapy has become more accessible — but low testosterone is rarely the
    only hormonal problem. Thyroid, cortisol, DHEA, growth hormone, and estradiol all
    degrade simultaneously in men over 35, compounding each other's effects on energy,
    mood, body composition, libido, recovery, and cognitive sharpness. TRT without a full
    panel is an incomplete answer to an incomplete question.
  </p>
  <p>
    Men's hormone replacement and hormone optimization require data. Multiple hormonal axes
    degrade in parallel: thyroid slows metabolic rate, elevated estradiol suppresses
    testosterone signaling, cortisol dysregulation burns out the HPA axis. The brain needs
    all of these in range. When they're not, no amount of willpower compensates.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Muscle pillar of the 4M framework treats hormone optimization as a foundational
    layer — because no training protocol, nutrition plan, or cognitive stack reaches its
