  <h2>The Insulting Behaviors</h2>
  <p>These are the most common ways men actively suppress their own hormonal function.</p>
  <ul class="insult-list">
    <li>No baseline lab work in the past 2 years — flying blind on your own biology</li>
    <li>Chronic sleep deprivation (under 7 hours) — testosterone is produced during deep sleep</li>
    <li>Chronic alcohol use — alcohol directly suppresses testosterone production</li>
    <li>Excess visceral body fat — fat tissue converts testosterone to estrogen</li>
    <li>Sedentary lifestyle with no resistance training — resistance training is the most reliable natural testosterone driver</li>
    <li>Daily exposure to endocrine disruptors: plastics, fluoride, common pesticide residues in food</li>
    <li>Chronic unmanaged stress — elevated cortisol directly suppresses testosterone synthesis</li>
  </ul>

